# Production build defaults.
#
# These override the untracked `.env` file, so `npm run build` always produces
# a same-origin bundle no matter which machine or CI runner does the building.
# Previously a developer's local `.env` (which points at the Render host for
# local development) was baked into `dist/`, which is how
# `https://eid-backend-4mrm.onrender.com` kept showing up inside the compiled
# JavaScript even though no source file hard-codes it.
#
# `/api` is correct for the container image, where nginx proxies it to the
# backend (see `deploy/nginx.conf.template`). If you deploy `dist/` as a static
# site instead, there is no proxy — set the absolute backend URL via the
# host's build-time environment variable for that deployment.
VITE_API_URL=/api
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
